1. Audit Objective — engagement-wide or control-specific?
When Section I states "Objective," is that meant to apply to every risk/control pairing tested under this APM, or does each control in Section III effectively have its own more specific objective that just isn't written out as a separate field? If a Test Objective needs to be checked for alignment "to the Audit Objective," should it always be checked against the single Section I statement, or is there a more granular objective implied per control?

2. Risk statement — is there a consistent narrative pattern in Section III?
Since Risk isn't a table column, is it always written as a heading or paragraph immediately above the control table it relates to? Or does the placement vary — e.g., sometimes one risk paragraph covers multiple controls, sometimes a risk is described after the table instead of before it? Knowing whether it's a consistent 1-risk-per-table pattern (versus something looser) determines whether extraction can be automated with confidence or needs a confirmation step every time.

